/Title (The first year WRO allowed open hardware meant learning everything from scratch, C++, sensor libraries, Arduino IDE, 3D printing custom parts in Tinkercad, and rewriting PID movement functions on entirely new hardware. New sensors like the HuskyLens added another layer to figure out. The steepest learning curve we'd faced. We came out National Champions with Top Score and Side Quest 4 \(Fastest time to complete a task\). Learn more about WRO25)
